---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 class="serif">A private companion for the days that are hard.</h1>
        <p class="hero-subhead">
          Tidelet helps you ride out cravings, track your relationship with alcohol,
          and see patterns you'd miss — all on your phone, with nothing ever sent
          anywhere else.
        </p>
        <a class="btn-primary" href="#download">Download on Google Play</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-mockup" aria-hidden="true">
        <!-- Replace with a real home-screen screenshot at /images/hero-home.webp -->
        <div class="phone-frame">
          <div class="phone-screen">
            <div class="phone-streak">7</div>
            <div class="phone-sublabel">days</div>
            <div class="phone-milestone">Next — 2 weeks · 7 to go</div>
            <div class="phone-sos">I'm having a craving</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <div class="how-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>1. Pick your starting date.</h3>
          <p>Today, yesterday, or any day. No account, no email.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>2. Open the SOS toolkit when a craving hits.</h3>
          <p>Ride the wave for 15 minutes. Try box breathing. Re-read your own reasons.
            Pick something else to do.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>3. Come back when you're ready.</h3>
          <p>See your own patterns. Keep what helps. Everything stays on your phone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What makes Tidelet different -->
  <section class="section-sunken">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What makes Tidelet different</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>On-device, always</h3>
          <p>Your data lives on your phone. No servers. No accounts. No syncing.
            We literally cannot see what you write, because we don't have a backend.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Grounded in research, not vibes</h3>
          <p>Every tool in Tidelet comes from cognitive behavioural therapy (CBT),
            Marlatt's relapse-prevention model, or urge surfing.
            The science is linked below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Anonymous by design</h3>
          <p>No email, no phone number, no sign-up. Open the app and you're in.
            The only identity Tidelet knows is the date you chose to start.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Free today</h3>
          <p>No ads. No in-app purchases. No subscription. If that ever changes,
            core features stay free — we'll tell you first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Compassionate about slips</h3>
          <p>A slip isn't a failure of you. Tidelet logs it, asks what helped and
            what didn't, and keeps your history. No streak-reset shame.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Quiet on purpose</h3>
          <p>No social feeds, no public badges, no daily push notifications trying
            to win your attention back. Tidelet is there when you need it and silent when you don't.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The science -->
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>The science</h2>
      <p>
        Tidelet's toolkit is built on techniques that clinical trials have shown to
        help people change their drinking:
      </p>
      <ul class="prose-list">
        <li>
          <strong>CBT (cognitive behavioural therapy) for alcohol use</strong> —
          the standard of care for mild-to-moderate alcohol problems, and the most
          consistently effective non-medication intervention in the research literature.
          Every thought check in Tidelet is a mini thought record.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Urge surfing</strong> — a mindfulness technique that turns a
          craving into an observed wave that rises and falls. Developed by
          Alan Marlatt and colleagues; validated in multiple RCTs for substance-use
          cravings. "Ride the wave" is a direct implementation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Marlatt's relapse-prevention model</strong> — high-risk situations,
          early warning signs, coping plan. Tidelet's compassionate-reset flow and
          functional-analysis prompts are built on this framework.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Distraction and alternative-activity scheduling</strong> — the
          behavioural lever behind "Do something else". Boring-sounding, and among
          the most durable interventions when practised.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="citations">
        Further reading: Kadden, Carroll et al., <em>Cognitive-Behavioral Coping Skills
        Therapy Manual</em> (NIAAA) · Marlatt & Donovan, <em>Relapse Prevention</em>
        (Guilford) · Bowen, Chawla, Marlatt, <em>Mindfulness-Based Relapse Prevention
        for Addictive Behaviors</em> · Beck & Liese, <em>Cognitive Therapy of Substance
        Abuse</em> (Guilford).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Privacy, really -->
  <section class="section-sunken">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Privacy, really</h2>
      <p>
        Most "private" apps mean "we encrypt what we collect." Tidelet doesn't
        collect anything. Here's what that actually means:
      </p>
      <ul class="prose-list">
        <li>The app <strong>does not request the INTERNET permission</strong> in
          its Android manifest. It literally cannot connect to the network.</li>
        <li><code>android:allowBackup="false"</code> — your data is not included in
          Google cloud backups unless you choose to export it.</li>
        <li>No third-party SDKs. No analytics. No crash reporting. No advertising IDs.</li>
        <li>No account, no email, no device fingerprint.</li>
        <li>Your data lives in a local Room database + DataStore file, on your
          phone only. For a backup, you export a Markdown file yourself and put it
          wherever you like.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What Tidelet is NOT -->
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>What Tidelet is <em>not</em></h2>
      <ul class="prose-list">
        <li>Not a replacement for therapy or medical care. If you're in crisis,
          please use the resources below.</li>
        <li>Not a social network. No leaderboards, no friends, no public streaks.</li>
        <li>Not a wellness subscription. No tiers, no premium, no "unlock insights
          for $9.99".</li>
        <li>Not a therapist. The tools inside are for self-guided practice
          between real support.</li>
        <li>Not an AI chatbot. There's nothing for the app to "learn" because nothing
          leaves your phone.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Crisis resources -->
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>If you're in crisis</h3>
        <p>
          Tidelet is a tool for the long, steady work of changing a habit. It is not
          crisis support. If you need someone right now:
        </p>
        <ul class="prose-list">
          <li><strong>United States</strong> — 988 (Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline);
            SAMHSA Helpline 1-800-662-4357</li>
          <li><strong>United Kingdom</strong> — Samaritans 116 123;
            Drinkline 0300 123 1110</li>
          <li><strong>India</strong> — iCall +91 9152987821; AASRA +91 9820466726</li>
          <li><strong>Elsewhere</strong> —
            <a href="https://findahelpline.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Find a Helpline</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section-sunken">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Is Tidelet really free?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. There are no ads, no in-app purchases, and no subscription. Core
          features will always be free. If we ever introduce an optional paid tier
          for non-essential extras, we'll tell you before anything changes.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I export my data?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. Settings → Export writes a Markdown file to a location you pick.
          You can re-import it later into a fresh install. The format is
          human-readable, so you can also read it in any text editor.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I slip?</summary>
        <p>
          Tidelet logs the slip, asks what was going on, and keeps your history.
          Your "days" counter reflects your current streak, but the events log keeps
          the full picture. Slips are data, not failures.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it only for alcohol?</summary>
        <p>
          Right now, yes. The tools (urge surfing, CBT thought checks, etc.)
          generalise to other compulsive behaviours, but the copy and defaults are
          built for alcohol. We'd rather do one thing well than four things vaguely.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it on iOS?</summary>
        <p>
          Not yet. Android-only. If we see strong interest and find the right iOS
          contributor, we'll consider it.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you have a privacy policy?</summary>
        <p>
          A one-page policy is linked in the footer. The short version: we don't
          collect data because the app has no way to.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I suggest a feature?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes, please email <a href="mailto:support@tidelet.app">support@tidelet.app</a>.
          We read everything. We reply when we can.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Download -->
  <section id="download" class="download-cta">
    <div class="container narrow" style="text-align: center;">
      <h2>Ready to start?</h2>
      <p style="margin-inline: auto;">
        Free download. No account. Your data stays on your phone.
      </p>
      <a class="btn-primary" href="#" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">Download on Google Play</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <div class="container footer-row">
      <span>© 2026 Tidelet</span>
      <span>
        <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy policy</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="mailto:support@tidelet.app">Support</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-12);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-display);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .hero-copy h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-5xl);
    }
  }

  .hero-subhead {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .hero-mockup {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Placeholder "phone" rendered in CSS so the page ships with no external
     image dependency. Swap for a real screenshot at public/images/hero-home.webp
     when ready — see LANDING_PAGE_SPEC.md §7.3. */
  .phone-frame {
    width: 260px;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 19.5;
    background: var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 10px;
  }

  .phone-screen {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--color-background);
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-lg) - 6px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .phone-streak {
    margin-top: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 5rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .phone-sublabel {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }

  .phone-milestone {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .phone-sos {
    margin-top: auto;
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-accent-warm);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    position: relative;
  }

  .phone-sos::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--space-4);
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--color-accent-warm);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  /* Three-column how-it-works. */
  .how-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .how-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .section-sunken {
    background: var(--color-surface-sunken);
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 42rem; /* 672 px — single-column reading width */
  }

  .prose-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .prose-list li {
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .citations {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .download-cta {
    padding-block: var(--space-12);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .footer-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
</style>
